  "caption": "Quinn runs five days a week and never lifts, convinced weights make runners slow. Then the niggles started queuing up — knee one week, calf the next.\n\nHeavier strength training can reduce overuse injuries and may make running more efficient, usually without much bulk.\n\nWhat can help: two 30–40 minute sessions a week, working knees, hips, calves, single-leg strength and trunk with challenging 4–8 rep sets built up gradually. Lift after easy runs, and give heavy calf raises priority.\n\nGet it checked if a niggle keeps hanging around or pain is changing the way you run — a physio can help adjust your plan.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
